This repository also contains third-party data: the antibody sequencing reads in the tests of
src/annotator.rs (module nt_tests_real), each a single read copied unchanged. They come from the
studies below, through the Observed Antibody Space database and the European Nucleotide Archive.

Observed Antibody Space (OAS), https://opig.stats.ox.ac.uk/webapps/oas/
  Available under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Olsen, Boyles & Deane (2022). Observed Antibody Space: A diverse database of cleaned, annotated,
    and translated unpaired and paired antibody sequences. Protein Science 31(1), 141-146.
    https://doi.org/10.1002/pro.4205
  Kovaltsuk et al. (2018). Observed Antibody Space: A Resource for Data Mining Next-Generation
    Sequencing of Antibody Repertoires. The Journal of Immunology 201(8), 2502-2509.
    https://doi.org/10.4049/jimmunol.1800708

European Nucleotide Archive (ENA), EMBL-EBI, https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ena/
  Raw reads of the sequencing runs behind some OAS data units, as their authors submitted them.

The original studies, by their name in OAS:

Alsoiussi_2020
  Alsoussi et al. (2020). A Potently Neutralizing Antibody Protects Mice against SARS-CoV-2
    Infection. The Journal of Immunology. https://doi.org/10.4049/jimmunol.2000583
  Data: OAS data unit SRR11528762_paired
  Tests: MOUSE_HEAVY, MOUSE_KAPPA, MOUSE_LAMBDA

